    "body": "The 4ms delay is for reentrant [timer tasks](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/timers-and-user-prompts.html#timer-initialisation-steps), i.e. for `setTimeout` (after 4 to 6 nesting levels).    \r\n\r\nAwaiting a microtask also takes some time, I'm not denying it, but it will be in *µs* not *ms*. My point is that your proposal would also execute tasks and microtasks, and pause / switch / resume the execution scripts, which will take the same amount of time as if you just awaited the queued task. I don't think this proposal avoids what actually costs performance.",
